<ArticleLayout slug="x-image-video-specs" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">X doesn't publish a pixel size for a post photo. It publishes a shape window and a weight cap. And three of its own pages disagree on how long a video can run.</p>

  <h2>What is the best X image size in 2026?</h2>

  <p>X image size in 2026 is a window, not a number. X's help center says a single photo shows in full anywhere from 2:1 to 3:4, up to 5MB, as a JPEG, PNG or GIF. A 16:9 frame sits well inside that window, and hubStudio's Image editor marks 1600 by 900 Best for an X post.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 14, 2026. Every number here comes from X's Help Center, X's ads creative specs or X's developer documentation, read directly that day, plus two dated X blog posts on how it crops images. The help and developer pages carry no date, so each row is dated by the read. Where two X pages disagree, both values are printed and each page is named.</p>

