  <blockquote class="evidence">X's help center says a single photo with a standard aspect ratio, from 2:1 to 3:4, "will display in full," and that what you see in the composer is what you get on X. Read directly from the help article, which carries no date.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: X Help Center, "How to post photos or GIFs on X," read October 14, 2026. https://help.x.com/en/using-x/posting-gifs-and-pictures</p>

  <p>Many size guides print 1200 by 675 as "the" X post size. You won't find it on X. None of the pages read for this guide gives a pixel size for a post photo; the pixels are your call, as long as the shape stays in the window.</p>

  <p>WebP is the one file conflict. X's developer documentation lists it; the consumer help article lists GIF, JPEG and PNG only. A JPEG or a PNG under 5MB clears both pages.</p>

  <h2>How does X crop a post with two, three or four pictures?</h2>

  <p>X doesn't say. Its pages give the four-item limit and the single-photo window, then point you to the composer preview. None of the X pages read for this guide describes how the timeline lays out or crops two, three or four pictures.</p>

