  <blockquote class="evidence">Three X pages give three ceilings for a long video. The video help article says under four hours at 1080p and 16GB for subscribers. The Premium page says about three hours and 8GB. The developer docs say 125 minutes and 16 GB through the API, and add that "Post-video caps match the X app."</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: X Help Center, "How to share and watch videos on X" and "About X Premium"; X developer documentation, "Media best practices"; read October 14, 2026. https://help.x.com/en/using-x/x-videos</p>

  <p>The build that clears every route: H.264 video with AAC audio, 1280 by 720 for landscape (or 720 by 720 square), 30 frames a second, under 140 seconds and under 512MB. Those are the codecs and frames X's developer docs recommend, and they sit inside the web limits too. X's organic help names no container; its ads specs take MP4 or MOV, so an MP4 is the safe export. The docs add that an account without a subscription gets 720p playback. Only subscribers get 1080p back.</p>

  <p>Two behaviors to plan for. Videos of 60 seconds or less loop. And Premium subscribers can download your video unless you switch off "Allow video to be downloaded" while composing; X's help says that setting can't be changed after the post goes out.</p>

