  <p>Ad copy follows the post rule, 280 characters, and each link takes 23 of them. X recommends a logo held in the upper left of a video ad, plus captions or text overlays. Not every format is open to self-serve advertisers, X notes. For the others, it points you to an account manager or a support ticket.</p>

  <h2>Why X uploads fail</h2>

  <p>Each cause below comes from X's own pages.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>The wrong file.</strong> BMP and TIFF are refused for posts and image ads.</li>
    <li><strong>A GIF that doesn't loop.</strong> X shows it as a still image. In an image ad, any uploaded GIF renders static.</li>
    <li><strong>An animated profile or header.</strong> Neither slot takes an animated GIF, X says.</li>
    <li><strong>A heavy profile photo.</strong> Over 2MB, it fails.</li>
    <li><strong>A video past the account's cap.</strong> Through the API, X refuses it at posting time ("This user is not allowed to post a video longer than N minutes"), even when the upload itself went through.</li>
    <li><strong>Changing your mind on downloads.</strong> The setting is fixed once the post is out. Delete and repost to change it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How hubStudio posts pictures to X</h2>

  <p>Connect your X account once on My Connections. Then, in the X module, pick a format (Text only, + Image, or + 2 to 4 pictures), write a brief and click Draft with AI, or Write it myself to type the post with no AI run. The X post format skill, picked by default, carries X's posting rules, and the counter counts 280 characters the way X does.</p>

  <p>Pictures come from a render, the Assets Library or an upload. Through hubStudio, X takes JPG, PNG, WebP and GIF up to 5 MB each; an animated GIF up to 15 MB goes out alone, as the only picture of its post.</p>

  <p>The pencil on a picture opens the Image editor on its Social panel, set to X. For a post it offers Post, wide (1600 by 900, marked Best), Post, square, Post, portrait and One of two; Header photo and Profile photo sit on the same list. Crop the picture or fit it whole over a blurred copy, and the editor shows in dashed lines how X crops it beside another picture. Editing is free.</p>

  <p>Publish now or schedule it, on up to 20 accounts. The queue is checked every five minutes, and each post is checked against X's limits again before it goes. A temporary error on X's side is retried, three attempts in all.</p>

  <p>Video is the exception. X takes no video from hubStudio yet, so a clip goes out through X's own composer, which the Publish manually tab opens with your copy in it. The <a href="/app/publish">publishing page of the app</a> covers the other networks.</p>

  <p>Each post sent to X through hubStudio is charged against your prepaid balance, and the price shows before you send. Posting it yourself in X's composer costs nothing. The <a href="/resources/insights/linkedin-post-specs">LinkedIn</a> and <a href="/resources/insights/instagram-post-sizes-2026">Instagram spec guides</a> in the <a href="/resources/specs">platform specs library</a> cover the other feeds. Teams that would rather hand the channel over can brief the <a href="/services/design/social-media">social media design service</a>.</p>

