  <h2>FAQ</h2>

  <h3>What is the best image size for X in 2026?</h3>

  <p>X gives no pixel size for a post photo. Its help center says a single photo shows in full anywhere from 2:1 to 3:4, up to 5MB, as a JPEG, PNG or GIF. A 16:9 landscape such as 1600 by 900 sits well inside that window and is the size hubStudio's Image editor marks Best for an X post.</p>

  <h3>How does X crop a post with several pictures?</h3>

  <p>X doesn't publish it. Its help center and developer docs give the limit, four items a post, and say a single photo between 2:1 and 3:4 shows in full. No X page read on October 14, 2026 describes the layout for two, three or four pictures. Keep each subject centered with margin, then check X's composer preview before posting.</p>

  <h3>How long can a video on X be?</h3>

  <p>On the web without a subscription, 140 seconds and 512MB, by X's video help. Premium subscribers get far more, but X's pages disagree on how much: under four hours and 16GB on the video help, about three hours and 8GB on the Premium page, 125 minutes through the API. Video ads run up to 2 minutes 20 seconds.</p>

  <h3>What is the X header photo size?</h3>

  <p>X recommends 1500 by 500 pixels for the header and 400 by 400 for the profile photo, as JPG, GIF or PNG, with no animated GIF in either slot. The profile photo caps at 2MB. X warns that 60 pixels at the top and bottom of the header could be cropped on some screens, so keep words in the middle.</p>

  <h3>What file types does X accept for images?</h3>

